Implementation should not start from this spec. The Gold row would let a wrong rate through, and the rounding rule isn't specified or tested. The author's "full coverage" claim doesn't hold. I did not edit any artefact.

```yaml
verdict: NEEDS_REWORK
confidence: medium
lenses:
  coverage:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "Gold total is 8400 in the feature but 8500 in AC-3 (subtotal 10000).", location: "discount.feature:16 vs ac.md:17"}
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "AC-4 (Bronze, 7 cents) has no scenario. test.md stops at AC-3 yet claims every criterion is covered.", location: "discount.feature; test.md:12"}
      - {gate: G2, severity: HIGH, finding: "No rounding or boundary subtotals. 10000 divides exactly at every tier.", location: "discount.feature:12-16"}
      - {gate: G1, severity: HIGH, finding: "AC-4 contradicts itself. Its title says rounding favours the customer, but 5% of 7 cents is 0.35 and charging 7 cents gives no reduction. The story owner must decide between 6 and 7 cents.", location: "ac.md:19-22"}
  business-alignment:
    status: pass
    findings: []
  testability:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G9, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "The outer test asserts Gold = 8_400, copying the feature's error. Spec and test agree, so the suite would go green on a wrong 16% rate.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:11"}
      - {gate: G10, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "No production code exists (CalculateLoyaltyDiscount, LoyaltyTier, query or quote types). The test fails on a compile error, not a business assertion, and no skeleton was written.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:1-16"}
      - {gate: G11, severity: HIGH, finding: "The test is in the UnitTest project but impl.md doesn't reference it. It covers AC-1 to AC-3 only.", location: "impl.md"}
      - {gate: G6, severity: HIGH, finding: "impl.md has no per-scenario entries, file paths or use-case boundary.", location: "impl.md:9-16"}
      - {gate: G5, severity: MEDIUM, finding: "'Rounded in the customer's favour' has no rule and no scenario pinning it.", location: "impl.md:11-12"}
  boundary-enforcement:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G7, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "contracts-{story}.md is missing, so CalculateLoyaltyDiscount.Handle can't be checked against a contract. The test does enter at the Application handler.", location: "details/2026-08-13/"}
      - {gate: G8, severity: HIGH, finding: "No walking skeleton scenario is identified.", location: "test.md:6-10"}
